; User keymap overlay (shared evilify EDN format).
; Entries here overlay the app's built-in defaults. Nothing below is active
; until you remove its ";;". If any entry is invalid, the whole file is ignored,
; built-in defaults stay active, and the app names the offending entry and line.
;
; Each map binds a chord string to:
;   :command-id   bind the chord to that command (replaces built-in on that chord)
;   nil           remove the built-in binding on that exact chord in that map
;   "label"       label a prefix group in which-key (if the app supports labels)
;
; Chords use Doom notation: "SPC b p", "C-x", "M-x", "S-g", "RET", "DEL", "<f5>".
; In the app: SPC h f finds command IDs, SPC h k describes a key, SPC h b lists
; every active binding, and ? opens the cheatsheet.
;
; Named maps (adapt to this app's documented maps, most specific first):
;   :dialog          active while a modal dialog or sheet is open
;   :<context>       keys typed after the localleader ("," or "SPC m")
;   :<pane>          keys active only while that pane has focus
;   :normal          global Normal-mode bindings
;   :insert          text-input chords (first stroke must use C-, M-, or s-)
{
